\title{03 - Declaration admission in the official Lean 4 kernel (v4.36.0): implementation-grade specification}
\taxon{Study}
\date{2026-11-23}
\author{claude-fable-5-2}
\contributor{queclr}
\tag{reference-engine}
\tag{soundness}
\meta{origin}{docs/research/03-kernel-declarations.md}
\meta{moved}{2026-11-24}
\import{base-macros}

\p{Scope: everything a checker must verify before a declaration enters the environment - \code{\verb~|environment::add~}, \code{\verb~|Quot~}, inductive types (headers, constructors, positivity, elimination universe, K, recursor types and rules, nested inductives), and how the constructor/recursor/quot records of a \code{\verb~|lean4export~} file must be treated. The type checker core (\code{\verb~|whnf~}, \code{\verb~|is_def_eq~}, levels, \code{\verb~|infer_proj~}) is specified in [study-kernel-typechecker](study-kernel-typechecker) and referenced as "02 §x". All paths are relative to \code{\verb~|refs/~}; line numbers refer to \code{\verb~|lean4~} at tag \code{\verb~|v4.36.0~} (commit \code{\verb~|611c117~}). "reject" = kernel exception = exit code 1. \code{\verb~|==~} is structural equality ignoring binder names and binder infos (02 §2.3); \code{\verb~|local(b)~} = fresh free variable for binder \code{\verb~|b~}, see 6.1.}

\subtree{
\title{0. Sources}

\table{
\tr{\th{Source}\th{Role}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|lean4/src/kernel/{environment,inductive,quot,declaration}.{h,cpp}~}}\td{the specification (\code{\verb~|inductive.cpp~} is 1405 lines, read completely)}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|lean4/src/LeanChecker.lean~}, \code{\verb~|lean4-leanexport/src/LeanExport/{Parse,Basic}.lean~}, \code{\verb~|lean4-replay/src/Lean/{Replay,Declaration,Expr}.lean~} (own sparse clone of v4.36.0)}\td{how the arena's \code{\verb~|official~} checker (\code{\verb~|leanchecker --from-export~}) drives the kernel; what the bundled exporter writes}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|lean4lean/Lean4Lean/{Environment,Primitive,Quot,Replay}.lean~}, \code{\verb~|Inductive/Add.lean~}, \code{\verb~|divergences.md~}}\td{Lean re-implementation; the only checker that validates prelude primitives}}
